      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the area of the figure \\(ABCD\\), we need to analyze the geometric shapes and their properties.\n\n1. **Identify the shape and its components:**\n   - The figure \\(ABCD\\) consists of two sectors of a circle with radius \\(12\\).\n   - Each sector has a central angle of \\(60^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Calculate the area of one sector:**\n   - The area \\(A\\) of a sector of a circle with radius \\(r\\) and central angle \\(\\theta\\) (in degrees) is given by:\n     \\[\n     A_{\\text{sector}} = \\frac{\\theta}{360^\\circ} \\times \\pi r^2\n     \\]\n   - Here, \\(r = 12\\) and \\(\\theta = 60^\\circ\\):\n     \\[\n     A_{\\text{sector}} = \\frac{60^\\circ}{360^\\circ} \\times \\pi \\times 12^2\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     A_{\\text{sector}} = \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\pi \\times 144\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     A_{\\text{sector}} = 24\\pi\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of two sectors:**\n   - Since the figure \\(ABCD\\) consists of two such sectors, the total area of the figure is:\n     \\[\n     A_{\\text{total}} = 2 \\times A_{\\text{sector}}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     A_{\\text{total}} = 2 \\times 24\\pi\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     A_{\\text{total}} = 48\\pi\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of figure \\(ABCD\\) is \\(\\boxed{48\\pi}\\).",
